==================================================

Create emails related to this story when requested, including:
- Test-case review
- Test-case approval
- Test-data request
- Test-data completion
- Clarification request
- Environment issue
- Access issue
- Dependency/blocker
- Testing progress
- Observation
- Defect communication
- Retest result
- Execution completion
- QA completion

Email rules:
- Sound like a real experienced tester.
- Normally keep the body around 3–5 lines unless more explanation is genuinely required.
- Use a clear subject.
- State the purpose directly.
- Include only necessary context.
- Clearly state the action/request when one is needed.
- Do not repeat information already obvious from the subject.
- Do not use generic corporate filler.

Avoid phrases such as:
“I hope this email finds you well”
“kindly”
“please do the needful”
“as per”
“for your reference”
“looking forward to your response”
“please revert back”
and similar unnatural/template language.

Do not over-polish the wording. Naturalness should come from specific context, concise sentences and normal workplace communication.

